WEBVTT

00:00:07.740 --> 00:00:13.660
in october 1967 soviet russia celebrated the 50th anniversary of the communist revolution

00:00:13.660 --> 00:00:18.650
nearly every major american magazine carried feature stories displaying the tremendous

00:00:18.650 --> 00:00:23.230
progress made by the communists in the fields of science industry and technology

00:00:23.230 --> 00:00:26.790
this segment of the news media was telling the american people

00:00:26.790 --> 00:00:29.600
that the communist system was enormously successful.

00:00:30.160 --> 00:00:34.960
if not wholly desirable. Honest history, however, presents a somewhat different picture of a nation

00:00:34.960 --> 00:00:41.720
that has, time after time, been saved from disaster through transfusions of food, money, and technology

00:00:41.720 --> 00:00:51.980
from the West, its avowed enemy. The Great Pretense, how to finance communism while ostensibly opposing it.

00:01:05.760 --> 00:01:11.020
The takeover of Russia by Bolshevism was not a spontaneous revolution of landless peasants and workers,

00:01:11.280 --> 00:01:16.100
but was a carefully designed plot, organized and financed from outside of Russia.

00:01:16.800 --> 00:01:18.800
Lenin was imported into Russia from Germany,

00:01:19.400 --> 00:01:23.240
and Leon Trotsky left his exile in New York City with a revolutionary cadre

00:01:23.240 --> 00:01:26.520
determined to make Russia the home of world communism.

00:01:27.710 --> 00:01:28.990
Revolutions are expensive.

00:01:29.350 --> 00:01:29.970
The money for the...

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:35.870
Bolshevik Revolution came primarily from Germany and the United States. One of the chief German

00:01:35.870 --> 00:01:41.640
financiers of the Russian Revolution was M. M. Warburg, who made millions available to the

00:01:41.640 --> 00:01:47.460
Russian communists through a bank in Sweden. In America, Jacob Schiff, a partner and brother-in-law

00:01:47.460 --> 00:01:53.240
of Warburg, contributed $20 million to the Russian Revolution. This was rather a strange

00:01:53.240 --> 00:01:57.670
act for an American, since it was definitely to the detriment of the United States to have

00:01:57.670 --> 00:01:59.970
Tsarist Russia knocked out of World War I.

00:02:00.470 --> 00:02:05.810
Three years after the revolution, Russia presented a picture of untilled fields and idle factories.

00:02:06.440 --> 00:02:07.360
All was chaos.

00:02:08.060 --> 00:02:12.060
Production had been reduced to one-seventh of the already low pre-war level.

00:02:12.780 --> 00:02:15.560
Such was the result of radical socialization.

00:02:15.970 --> 00:02:19.010
In order to save communism, Lenin ordered a complete about-face.

00:02:19.660 --> 00:02:23.880
In 1921, he announced his new economic policy, known as NEP.

00:02:24.670 --> 00:02:29.970
Lenin called upon the mighty industrial powers of the West with their engineers, research scientists, and technologists.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:36.300
technologists to come to Russia so that Bolshevik progress might begin. Lenin said of the hated

00:02:36.300 --> 00:02:42.060
capitalists, quote, they will furnish credits which will serve as a means to support the communist

00:02:42.060 --> 00:02:47.320
parties, and by supplying us with materials and techniques which are not available to us,

00:02:47.650 --> 00:02:53.180
they will rebuild our war industry, which is essential to our future attacks on our own

00:02:53.180 --> 00:02:59.970
suppliers. In other words, they will be laboring to prepare their own suicide. Lenin was right.

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:05.340
for the West took the bait. Historian Werner Keller, in his excellent book, East minus West

00:03:05.340 --> 00:03:10.990
equals zero, describes how capitalism built communism. The first modern aircraft factory

00:03:10.990 --> 00:03:16.600
in Russia was built by the German Junkers concern. Thus, Soviet air power was born. Large

00:03:16.600 --> 00:03:21.200
numbers of Soviet engineers and workers were trained. Many hundreds of Russian pilots were

00:03:21.200 --> 00:03:26.470
thoroughly instructed by German test pilots, and the first Russian airline network was created.

00:03:26.890 --> 00:03:29.850
Eventually, the Soviets began to cold shoulder the Junkers people.

00:03:30.320 --> 00:03:33.440
exactly as they would do in the case of other concessionaires

00:03:33.440 --> 00:03:36.500
when the foreigners from the West had fulfilled their function.

00:03:37.260 --> 00:03:41.940
After 1925, the USSR began withdrawing one concession after another

00:03:41.940 --> 00:03:45.800
and breaking the agreements made in their original contracts.

00:03:46.450 --> 00:03:48.510
The Red Army was also built by Germany.

00:03:48.990 --> 00:03:54.110
Because Germany was forbidden by the Versailles Treaty to maintain an army or to manufacture arms,

00:03:54.640 --> 00:03:57.920
Communist Russia offered Germany a unique chance to evade the treaty.

00:03:58.730 --> 00:03:59.970
Moscow willingly made...

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:05.080
suitable training areas available to the German army so that it might continue undisturbed behind

00:04:05.080 --> 00:04:11.340
the Iron Curtain by developing and testing its weapons on maneuvers. The Germans established a

00:04:11.340 --> 00:04:16.140
flying school, an armored vehicle school, and a chemical warfare research unit within Russia.

00:04:16.900 --> 00:04:21.380
Large-scale production of new tanks and military aircrafts were begun by the Germans in Russian

00:04:21.380 --> 00:04:27.270
factories. German officers secretly trained the Red Army, including many of Russia's future generals.

00:04:27.900 --> 00:04:29.940
Russia's most famous general, Reg.

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:33.560
was himself a product of German staff schools.

00:04:33.860 --> 00:04:36.820
Ultramodern gold mining installations were constructed in Russia

00:04:36.820 --> 00:04:39.660
by Lina Goldfields Limited, an English firm.

00:04:40.400 --> 00:04:43.490
As soon as the gold field was developed, the English were ousted.

00:04:44.140 --> 00:04:48.040
The gold mine from the Lina field by hundreds of thousands of slave laborers

00:04:48.060 --> 00:04:51.220
provided much of the money with which Russia paid the capitalists

00:04:51.560 --> 00:04:55.160
for building the industrial capacity of the USSR.

00:04:56.100 --> 00:04:59.640
Other foreign exchange money was obtained by deliberately starving to death

00:05:00.160 --> 00:05:04.830
millions of russians so that wheat could be exported the united states has been russia's

00:05:04.830 --> 00:05:10.560
prime patron ever since the russian revolution in 1921 herbert hoover set up an international

00:05:10.560 --> 00:05:17.620
organization to end famine in russia the united states alone sent 700 000 tons of foodstuffs

00:05:17.620 --> 00:05:24.230
this was a prime example of misplaced idealism and charity while many lives were saved the

00:05:24.280 --> 00:05:29.980
communist system was also saved with the result that millions have lost their lives and the russia

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:35.530
The Russian people were deprived of their best opportunity to throw off the yoke of their slave masters.

00:05:35.790 --> 00:05:39.170
Even though there were no diplomatic relations between Moscow and Washington,

00:05:39.660 --> 00:05:42.900
American industrialists made private agreements with the Soviet Union.

00:05:43.620 --> 00:05:46.240
Thus, U.S. firms acquired gold prospecting rights.

00:05:46.600 --> 00:05:49.320
The Standard Oil Company won an oil-boring concession.

00:05:49.940 --> 00:05:53.080
Averill Harriman built mines to work manganese ore deposits.

00:05:53.730 --> 00:05:58.470
General Electric sold Moscow electrical equipment to the value of over $20 million.

00:05:58.470 --> 00:05:59.970
and other Americans

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:07.570
firms set about re-equipping Russian industry. From 1921 to 1925, 37 million

00:06:07.570 --> 00:06:11.930
dollars of machinery and equipment were pumped into the Soviet economy by

00:06:12.050 --> 00:06:17.150
American industry. In 1928, the NEP was replaced by the first five-year plan,

00:06:17.350 --> 00:06:21.930
which promised to transform the Soviet Union from an agricultural into an

00:06:21.930 --> 00:06:26.740
industrial economy. Such a vast project was impossible without the active help

00:06:26.830 --> 00:06:29.550
of Western industry and its unlimited supplies.

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:31.540
and expert technical knowledge.

00:06:32.230 --> 00:06:33.990
By the time the first plan was announced,

00:06:34.380 --> 00:06:37.700
the essential contracts had already been signed by Western firms,

00:06:37.920 --> 00:06:42.280
which was why the Soviets appeared so confident in projecting their goals.

00:06:42.860 --> 00:06:44.460
Unobserved by the American public,

00:06:44.680 --> 00:06:47.200
some of the largest American industrial concerns,

00:06:47.220 --> 00:06:50.440
which were steadily insulted in the Soviet press as, quote,

00:06:50.880 --> 00:06:53.800
the last strongholds of imperialist capitalism,

00:06:54.590 --> 00:06:56.610
began doing business with the communists.

00:06:57.140 --> 00:06:59.860
Orders worth millions of dollars poured into the offices.

00:07:00.150 --> 00:07:01.630
of these great firms.

00:07:02.710 --> 00:07:05.990
In 1930, the Bolsheviks arranged for the Ford Motor Company

00:07:05.990 --> 00:07:08.530
to establish the Russian motor car industry.

00:07:09.240 --> 00:07:12.240
The Soviet representatives signed contracts with Henry Ford

00:07:12.240 --> 00:07:15.420
for patent licenses, technical assistance and advice,

00:07:15.780 --> 00:07:18.260
plus an inventory of spare parts.

00:07:18.650 --> 00:07:21.250
Ford technicians were sent to Russia to train the Russians

00:07:21.250 --> 00:07:22.930
in assembling automobiles.

00:07:23.380 --> 00:07:27.400
The factory was to be capable of turning out 140,000 cars a year,

00:07:27.540 --> 00:07:29.900
and an Ohio construction company...

00:07:29.900 --> 00:07:29.980
Thank you.

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:35.520
to build the factory. The town of Gorky was transformed into the Detroit of

00:07:35.520 --> 00:07:40.350
Russia. The Russian steel industry is another example of Russian power made in

00:07:40.350 --> 00:07:45.910
the USA. A Cleveland firm contracted to do nothing less than rebuild a copy of

00:07:46.030 --> 00:07:50.880
the city of Gary, Indiana, the center of American iron and steel industry on

00:07:51.130 --> 00:07:56.740
Russian soil. This was to be the huge Soviet steel complex Magnatogorsk.

00:07:57.370 --> 00:07:59.110
Without iron, there can be no steel.

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:06.020
Steel, no heavy industry, and without heavy industry, no Bolshevik power to bury the West.

00:08:06.700 --> 00:08:11.280
Americans made Magnetogorsk the biggest iron and steel works in the world.

00:08:12.000 --> 00:08:15.000
Tractors were a necessity to modernize Soviet agriculture.

00:08:15.420 --> 00:08:20.920
A Detroit engineer designed and constructed a tractor factory without parallel in any other country.

00:08:21.460 --> 00:08:27.530
The assembly works were 2,000 feet long and 650 feet wide, covering an area of 30 acres.

00:08:28.210 --> 00:08:29.970
The tractors produced were copies of the American...

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:34.190
Caterpillar Company, but there were no arrangements made for payment for use of

00:08:34.190 --> 00:08:39.590
the patent. Russia merely bought one sample and copied it. The factory was so

00:08:39.590 --> 00:08:43.440
designed that production could be adapted almost overnight to the

00:08:43.440 --> 00:08:50.280
production of another less innocuous commodity, tanks. The communists achieved a

00:08:50.280 --> 00:08:54.360
propaganda victory by distributing millions of pictures around the globe of

00:08:54.540 --> 00:08:58.610
the world's largest hydroelectric installation and dam at Niprogus.

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:05.410
a classic of communist development. Actually, it represented the peak of American achievement.

00:09:06.080 --> 00:09:11.240
It was designed and built by Colonel Hugh Cooper, who built the dam at Muscle Shoals, Tennessee.

00:09:12.140 --> 00:09:18.330
The power plant increased Russia's hydroelectric system output by six times and produced more power

00:09:18.330 --> 00:09:25.590
than Niagara Falls. Still, by 1933, Russia was once again on the verge of collapse. And again,

00:09:25.690 --> 00:09:29.980
it was America which saved the communist regime, this time through official diplomatic...

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:35.050
recognition of the communists. On the verge of financial collapse, Russia had been staying alive

00:09:35.050 --> 00:09:40.420
by what amounted to the kiting of checks on an international level. When President Franklin D.

00:09:40.540 --> 00:09:45.120
Roosevelt reversed the position of four other United States presidents and recognized the

00:09:45.120 --> 00:09:49.760
legitimacy of the communist government, the prestige and thereby the credit of the communists

00:09:49.920 --> 00:09:56.180
skyrocketed overnight. In return for recognition, Maxine Litvinoff promised FDR that the American

00:09:56.180 --> 00:09:59.500
communists would cease calling for the overthrow of the United States government.

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:03.080
and the establishment of a red dictatorship in America.

00:10:03.500 --> 00:10:05.720
It was not until the advent of World War II

00:10:05.720 --> 00:10:08.380
that the anti-American propaganda was played down

00:10:08.380 --> 00:10:09.960
in the American communist press,

00:10:10.500 --> 00:10:12.960
which at that time had a circulation of millions.

00:10:13.840 --> 00:10:18.500
Ignoring the Russian invasion of Poland, Latvia, Estonia, Lithuania, and Finland,

00:10:18.880 --> 00:10:21.080
the American government and the American press

00:10:21.080 --> 00:10:25.060
heralded the Soviets as great believers in liberty and democracy

00:10:25.060 --> 00:10:26.640
during World War II.

00:10:27.480 --> 00:10:29.960
In view of the communist unbroken record of...

00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:34.400
for world conquest by communist imperialism there was no reason why

00:10:34.400 --> 00:10:38.900
anyone in America should have been so fooled but once again the United States

00:10:38.900 --> 00:10:43.830
saved the Soviet Union from destruction through the medium of lend-lease while

00:10:44.400 --> 00:10:48.240
many Americans felt the world's two worst criminal dictators Hitler and

00:10:48.240 --> 00:10:52.590
Stalin should be allowed to fight each other to the death America intervened

00:10:52.590 --> 00:10:57.400
with all its might on the side of the red dictator a man in charge of Russian

00:10:57.400 --> 00:10:59.490
Lend-Lease was the mysterious

00:10:59.490 --> 00:10:59.970
Harry

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:05.940
Hopkins, the alter ego of Franklin D. Roosevelt, who actually lived in the White House. Writer

00:11:05.940 --> 00:11:10.440
historian William Henry Chamberlain has written that Hopkins was, quote, after the president,

00:11:10.840 --> 00:11:15.860
the most powerful man in America during the war. Hopkins, at a Russian aid rally in Madison

00:11:15.860 --> 00:11:21.900
Square Garden in June 1942, said, quote, we are determined that nothing shall stop us from

00:11:21.900 --> 00:11:29.020
sharing with you all that we have. Major General John Dean, an expert on Russian lend-lease, said

00:11:29.020 --> 00:11:29.920
that Hopkins designed

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:35.300
to help the Russians was, quote, carried out with a zeal which approached fanaticism.

00:11:36.020 --> 00:11:40.760
Materials destined for General MacArthur in the South Pacific were rerouted to Russia

00:11:40.760 --> 00:11:43.210
through the influence of Harry Hopkins.

00:11:43.570 --> 00:11:47.110
In letters to American agencies dated March 7, 1942,

00:11:47.550 --> 00:11:51.290
President Roosevelt ordered that preferential position in matters of munitions

00:11:51.290 --> 00:11:55.140
should be given to the Soviet Union over all other allies

00:11:55.140 --> 00:11:59.050
and even the armed forces of the United States.

00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:05.960
General Dean later wrote that, then and there was, quote, the beginning of a policy of appeasement

00:12:05.960 --> 00:12:11.840
of Russia from which we have never recovered and from which we are still suffering. American help

00:12:11.840 --> 00:12:16.830
went to the Soviet Union at a crucial moment. It is officially estimated that the U.S. sent the

00:12:16.830 --> 00:12:24.150
USSR over 11 billion dollars in goods, plus the cost of transportation to Russia. Russia, of

00:12:24.150 --> 00:12:29.080
course, has never repaid a single cent. Vice President Henry Wallace addressed the American

00:12:29.080 --> 00:12:29.980
people overrated.

00:12:30.000 --> 00:12:37.320
on July 9, 1944, after returning from a trip to Russia. He gloated, quote, I found American flour

00:12:37.320 --> 00:12:43.560
in the Soviet Far East, American aluminum in Soviet airplane factories, American steel in trucks and

00:12:43.560 --> 00:12:49.420
railway repair shops, American machine tools in shipbuilding yards, American compressors and

00:12:49.420 --> 00:12:55.280
electrical equipment on Soviet naval vessels, American electric shovels in open-cut coal mines,

00:12:55.750 --> 00:12:59.980
American core drills in the copper mines of Central Asia, and American...

00:13:00.000 --> 00:13:03.800
trucks, and planes performing strategic transportation functions.

00:13:04.140 --> 00:13:06.920
Over half the value of goods sent were non-munitions.

00:13:07.400 --> 00:13:10.440
The variety of goods shipped to Russia runs into the thousands,

00:13:10.500 --> 00:13:13.360
consisting of almost every product imaginable.

00:13:13.860 --> 00:13:17.320
It has been called the greatest mail-order catalog in history.

00:13:17.950 --> 00:13:21.550
What did America send to Russia between 1941 and 1945?

00:13:22.620 --> 00:13:28.220
2,660 ships with a total cargo of 16.25 million tons

00:13:28.220 --> 00:13:29.970
left American ports for...

00:13:30.000 --> 00:13:36.230
Soviet Union. America donated over 15,000 planes to the Soviets. The Russian

00:13:36.230 --> 00:13:40.270
transportation system, which had almost broken down, was completely re-equipped.

00:13:40.900 --> 00:13:47.250
1900 steam locomotives and 66 diesels were sent by the U.S. together with 10,000

00:13:47.250 --> 00:13:52.760
railway cars, shipload after shipload of machine tools, complete industrial plants,

00:13:53.140 --> 00:13:57.800
spare parts and armaments, textiles and footwear were unloaded in Russian ports.

00:13:58.110 --> 00:13:59.970
of inestimable value were

00:14:00.000 --> 00:14:06.300
the supplies of foodstuffs. Nearly four and one half million tons of tin meat, sugar, flour, and

00:14:06.300 --> 00:14:11.660
fats were sent from America. Gold mining equipment from American mines, which had been closed by

00:14:11.660 --> 00:14:16.740
government orders, were shipped to the Russians at the express orders of the Treasury Department's

00:14:16.740 --> 00:14:25.190
Harry Dexter White, who was later proven by the FBI to be a Soviet spy. According to Victor

00:14:25.190 --> 00:14:29.970
Kravchenko, who defected from the Soviet Union after serving in America during World War II,

00:14:30.760 --> 00:14:34.520
All Russian personnel sent to this country during the war had two jobs.

00:14:34.860 --> 00:14:38.750
First, his regular job, and second, that of being a spy.

00:14:39.570 --> 00:14:43.650
Among the agents posing as unimportant minor officials were famous scientists

00:14:43.650 --> 00:14:46.830
and high-ranking officers with special technical qualification.

00:14:47.680 --> 00:14:51.060
Some of the Soviet experts were camouflaged as ordinary workmen.

00:14:51.700 --> 00:14:56.930
Their job was the theft of technical and scientific secrets from American industrial concern.

00:14:57.460 --> 00:14:59.960
The headquarters of the Soviet espionage ring...

00:15:00.000 --> 00:15:04.520
was in Washington in the Soviet Purchasing Commission called Amtorg, which was officially

00:15:04.520 --> 00:15:09.000
concerned with administering lend-lease. The government watched the activities of the Soviet

00:15:09.000 --> 00:15:13.630
agents with incredible tolerance. The worst that could happen to an agent was a polite

00:15:13.630 --> 00:15:18.900
request that he leave the country. In such cases, an official of the FBI would accompany

00:15:18.900 --> 00:15:24.600
the agent to the boat or plane leaving for Moscow, but without checking his luggage or

00:15:24.600 --> 00:15:29.730
briefcase. Among the items obtained by Amtorg spies were designs of industrial plants.

00:15:30.000 --> 00:15:35.280
Special machines, parts and details, photographs and blueprints of technical processes in aviation,

00:15:35.720 --> 00:15:38.800
arms, oil, submarine building, and many other industries.

00:15:38.800 --> 00:15:46.250
Plus, complete maps of the United States and locations of strategic defense plants and military installations.

00:15:47.360 --> 00:15:51.780
The technical information stolen by the Russians was worth hundreds of millions of dollars.

00:15:52.120 --> 00:15:58.980
The tens of tons of stolen documents, plans, and other technical data were shipped to Russia across the Arctic by airplane.

00:15:59.130 --> 00:15:59.970
Our pact

00:16:00.000 --> 00:16:05.270
into the holes of Soviet cargo ships with no customs inspection because they had diplomatic

00:16:05.270 --> 00:16:10.470
immunity. With tools, machinery, or apparatus too heavy or too bulky for this procedure,

00:16:10.990 --> 00:16:15.220
the Soviets developed another technique. The goods were declared as something other than

00:16:15.220 --> 00:16:20.050
what they were. For example, secret radar sets were declared as truck engines which

00:16:20.050 --> 00:16:24.970
were permitted exports under Lend-Lease. Tens of thousands of patents were copied and

