were under development, but also the State Department issued an order allowing the...

00:17:00.000 --> 00:17:05.860
Russians to visit any restricted industrial plant and to take motion pictures of intricate machinery

00:17:05.860 --> 00:17:12.210
and manufacturing processes. FBI reports on all of this piled up in Washington, but the government

00:17:12.210 --> 00:17:17.950
kept these reports confidential and did nothing about it. One of the first persons to expose this

00:17:17.950 --> 00:17:24.040
incredible story was Major George Racy Jordan, who in 1949, before a congressional committee,

00:17:24.280 --> 00:17:29.700
revealed diaries that he had kept while in charge of expediting lend-lease to Russia from the giant

00:17:29.700 --> 00:17:29.980
And...

00:17:30.000 --> 00:17:34.940
Falls Montana Air Base. Major Jordan had kept meticulous records to the

00:17:34.940 --> 00:17:38.280
unbelievable manner in which the Russians were allowed to ship goods and

00:17:38.280 --> 00:17:42.860
documents out of the country. Many of the cargo planes which left Great Falls

00:17:42.860 --> 00:17:48.040
contained three to four thousand pounds of mail for the Soviet Union. Americans

00:17:48.040 --> 00:17:51.140
were not allowed to inspect these consignments which were carried in large

00:17:51.140 --> 00:17:56.140
cheap black suitcases and accompanied by two guards under order to ensure there

00:17:56.140 --> 00:17:59.850
There were no jets, the event which motivated Major Jordan.

00:18:00.000 --> 00:18:05.740
To make his diaries available was the explosion in September 1949 of an atom bomb by the Soviets.

00:18:06.500 --> 00:18:12.460
Major Jordan testified that included among the shipments of strategic goods out of Great Falls to Russia

00:18:12.460 --> 00:18:15.130
were quantities of heavy water and uranium.

00:18:16.040 --> 00:18:19.120
At the time, Major Jordan, like almost all other Americans,

00:18:19.560 --> 00:18:22.580
knew nothing of the significance of heavy water and uranium.

00:18:23.250 --> 00:18:25.770
He had been ordered over the telephone by Harry Hopkins

00:18:25.770 --> 00:18:29.980
to expedite certain experimental chemicals to Russia and leave...

00:18:30.000 --> 00:18:34.890
it off the records. This was uranium ore, which was shipped from Canada. The bills of lading are

